From 7a8bcd40459cdbf429ed7852e5ac1b2e2effd42b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mingyang Sun (Public)" <mingsun@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 07:50:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] fix(clr): drop redundant OCP conjunction from the
 block16 guards

Review feedback: HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_BLOCK16_BUILTINS alone is sufficient.

  HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS     = __gfx1250__ || __gfx1250_strict__
  HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_BLOCK16_BUILTINS = __gfx1250__

so BLOCK16 implies OCP and the conjunction is always redundant. Both
macros are defined in exactly two places (amd_hip_mx_common.h and
amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp), identically in each, and neither is ever #undef'd
or redefined, so the implication holds for every translation unit.

Simplifies 30 guards: 8 in amd_hip_fp4.h, 12 in amd_hip_fp6.h and 10 in
amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp.

No functional change. Verified by compiling an fp4/fp6 conversion TU with
--cuda-device-only and diffing the device ISA before and after: identical
for both targets (only the path-derived __hip_cuid_ module hash moves).
gfx1250 keeps 4 cvt_scale_pk + 2 cvt_scalef32_pk in 50 instructions;
gfx1250-strict keeps 0 cvt_scale_pk + 2 cvt_scalef32_pk in 167, i.e. the
software fallback for the unpack direction is still selected there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 195db54a098d1aa2ad44a3b4e8d88c86800e822f)
